#X text 551 374 The [avg~] object will connect to the [print] object. However \, when the audio DSP is on \, the changes that occur to the output appear to be instantaneous. I cannot see the scrolling up of the change from 0 to 1 or back to 0 The refresh rate on the print in this case must be very high because it is a signal. Printing in this case might be hard on the CPU.;
#X obj 627 494 print -n;
#X text 730 473 To suppress the print prefeix when there is no user prefix \, you can add a -n to the [print] object. If there is a user prefix \, adding a -n just makes it part of the prefix.;
#X text 730 525 DISCONNECT [print]'s SO THEY DO NOT RUN ALL THE TIME.;
#X text 685 55 The ~ with the && makes the number a signal and you use the [avg~] to process that. The help file for [avg~] says that it "calculates the arithemtic mean of one signal vector." I wonder what that means when you see the examples to the left. I am working on what I see in the Help examples. So I will provide that here too.;
