#X text 876 160 Without doing some reading and brushing up on trig math \, the average of a changing waveform is not calculated the same way as the average of a group of non-changing numbers.;
#X text 1191 288 TO SEE BETTER EXAMPLES \, RIGHT CLICK ON THE [&&~] OBJECT AND SELECT;
#X text 1191 288 TO SEE BETTER EXAMPLES \, RIGHT CLICK ON THE [&&~] OBJECT AND SELECT HELP. LOGIC STILL APPLIES BUT WHEN YOU USE NON-CHANGING NUMBERS INSTEAD OF WAVEFORMS \, YOU WILL GET DIFFERENT RESULTS THAN WITH WAVEFORMS.;
