#X text 483 1216 The answer to the question at the top of this section lies in the fact that the [>~ 2] object will not connect with the number box below it. The [avg~] is needed to connect those two things so we can see the result. I do not know why. Maybe the logic operation produces a result that is no longer a number and the [avg~] object makes it a number again.;
#X obj 1152 1321 print value from >~ 2;
